# SteamOS Configuration with Distrobox

This directory contains SteamOS-specific configurations optimized for development using Distrobox containers.

## Development Strategy: Distrobox Approach

### Why Distrobox?
- **Space Efficient**: Keeps host system minimal, uses unlimited container space
- **Persistent**: Survives SteamOS updates
- **Flexible**: Run any Linux distro (Ubuntu, Fedora, Arch) alongside SteamOS
- **Integrated**: Seamless file access between host and container

### Architecture Overview
```
SteamOS Host (Minimal)          Ubuntu Container (Full Dev)
├── git, neovim, tmux          ├── All development languages
├── zsh, basic tools           ├── VS Code, IDEs, browsers  
├── Distrobox                  ├── Docker, databases
└── ~/.local/share/chezmoi     └── Full chezmoi environment
```

## Quick Start

### 1. Initial Setup
```bash
# Run chezmoi to setup host system + Distrobox
chezmoi apply

# Enter development container
distrobox enter dev

# Setup full development environment in container
setup-dev-container
chezmoi init
chezmoi apply
```

### 2. Daily Workflow
```bash
# Enter development container
distrobox enter dev

# Your files are in ~/Development (shared with host)
cd ~/Development/personal
code .

# Exit back to host
exit
```

## Benefits Over Traditional Approach

| Aspect | Traditional SteamOS | Distrobox Approach |
|--------|-------------------|-------------------|
| Root Space Usage | ~1-2GB packages | ~200MB minimal tools |
| Development Space | Limited by root partition | Unlimited (home partition) |
| Update Persistence | Lost on SteamOS updates | Survives all updates |
| Package Management | pacman (read-only issues) | apt/dnf (normal Linux) |
| IDE Support | Limited by space | Full VS Code, IDEs |

## Configuration Files

### Host System (Minimal)
- **Konsole Profile**: Victor Mono font with Steam Deck optimizations
- **Tmux Config**: Handheld-optimized settings for host system
- **Shell Setup**: Basic zsh with Starship prompt
- **Git Config**: Basic git configuration

### Container Environment (Full)
- **Development Languages**: Node.js, Python, Go, Rust, Lua
- **Modern CLI Tools**: ripgrep, fd, bat, exa, zoxide
- **Development Tools**: Docker, databases, build tools
- **Editor Integration**: Full VS Code, neovim setup

## Installation Process

### 1. Host Setup (`run_onchange_steamos-install-packages.sh`)
- Installs minimal essential tools (~200MB)
- Installs and configures Distrobox
- Creates Ubuntu development container
- Sets up container entry scripts

### 2. Container Setup (`run_onchange_ubuntu-dev-container.sh`)
- Installs full development environment
- Configures modern CLI tools
- Sets up Oh My Zsh and aliases
- Creates development directory structure

### 3. Font & Desktop (`run_once_steamos-setup.sh`)
- Installs Victor Mono Nerd Font
- Configures Konsole terminal
- Sets up desktop shortcuts

## Container Commands

### Management
```bash
distrobox list                    # List containers
distrobox enter dev              # Enter development container
distrobox create --name test --image fedora:39  # Create new container
distrobox rm dev                 # Remove container
```

### Development Workflow
```bash
# Quick development session
distrobox enter dev
cd ~/Development/myproject
code .                           # VS Code in container
npm run dev                      # Development server

# Container commands are available in host
distrobox-export --app code      # Export VS Code to host menu
```

## File System Layout

### Host System
```
/home/deck/
├── .local/share/chezmoi/        # Chezmoi source (host config)
├── .config/                     # Host system configs
└── Development/                 # Shared development folder
```

### Container System  
```
/home/deck/  (same home directory)
├── Development/                 # Same files as host
├── .local/share/chezmoi/        # Container-specific chezmoi
└── container-specific configs   # Full development setup
```

## Troubleshooting

### Container Issues
```bash
# Recreate container if corrupted
distrobox rm dev
distrobox create --name dev --image ubuntu:22.04
distrobox enter dev
setup-dev-container

# Check container status
distrobox list
podman ps -a
```

### Space Management
```bash
# Host system cleanup
sudo pacman -Scc
sudo journalctl --vacuum-time=1d

# Container cleanup (inside container)
sudo apt autoremove
sudo apt autoclean
```

